  },
  {
   "id": "tt012t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 270,
   "y": 1320,
   "w": 460,
   "h": 25.2,
   "text": "What Tomatone is",
   "weight": 700
  },
  {
   "id": "tt013t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 270,
   "y": 1370,
   "w": 698,
   "h": 120,
   "text": "Your playlist, turned into a clock you can hear, and over time, one you can sense.",
   "size": "l",
   "bg": "accent"
  },
  {
   "id": "tt014t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 270,
   "y": 1560,
   "w": 460,
   "h": 80,
   "text": "Tomatone is a single-purpose musical timer that translates the passage of time into an evolving auditory experience. Instead of an abrasive buzzer or a countdown clock, your playlist and an underlying pulse speed up as your deadline nears. Through repeated exposure, users learn to recognise and internalise the musical cues, gradually developing an intuitive relationship with time.",
   "size": "s"
  },
  {
   "id": "tt015p",
   "type": "image",
   "x": 270,
   "y": 1680,
   "w": 341,
   "h": 340,
   "src": "projects/media/tomatone/photo-palm.jpg",
   "fit": "cover",
   "alt": "Tomatone resting in an open palm",
   "round": 8,
   "zoom": true,
   "caption": "Screenless form factor held in hand.",
   "capShow": true
  },
  {
   "id": "tt016p",
   "type": "image",
   "x": 627,
   "y": 1680,
   "w": 341,
   "h": 340,
   "src": "projects/media/tomatone/photo-button.jpg",
   "fit": "cover",
   "alt": "Finger pressing olive button on top of Tomatone",
   "round": 8,
   "zoom": true,
   "caption": "Olive-green top button for pairing and silent haptic mode.",
   "capShow": true
  },
  {
   "id": "tt017t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 270,
   "y": 2080,
   "w": 460,
   "h": 45,
   "text": "Why a tomato? The name, the red colour, and the kitchen vocabulary come from the Pomodoro Technique, which was originally named after a tomato-shaped kitchen timer.",
   "size": "s",
   "color": "mute"
  },
  {
   "id": "tt020t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 32,
   "y": 2260,
   "w": 222,
   "h": 25.2,
   "text": "brief & words",
   "color": "mute",
   "nav": "brief & words"
  },
  {
   "id": "tt021t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 270,
   "y": 2260,
   "w": 460,
   "h": 25.2,
   "text": "Map, Extend, Panoramic",
   "weight": 700
  },
  {
   "id": "tt022t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 270,
   "y": 2305,
   "w": 460,
   "h": 40,
   "text": "The prompt asked to pick a noun, an adjective, and a verb from a random generator, define a problem, and design a solution.",
   "size": "s"
  },
  {
   "id": "tt023g",
   "type": "group",
   "x": 270,
   "y": 2370,
   "w": 222,
   "h": 125,
   "children": [
    {
     "id": "tt023a",
     "type": "text",
     "x": 0,
     "y": 0,
     "w": 222,
     "h": 19.3,
     "text": "01 / Noun",
     "size": "s",
     "color": "mute"
    },
    {
     "id": "tt023b",
     "type": "text",
     "x": 0,
     "y": 20,
     "w": 222,
     "h": 22,
     "text": "MAP",
     "weight": 700
    },
    {
     "id": "tt023c",
     "type": "text",
     "x": 0,
     "y": 46,
     "w": 222,
     "h": 68,
     "text": "Shape, route, trace, plan. Mapping the structure of a session across the day.",
     "size": "s"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "tt024g",
   "type": "group",
   "x": 508,
   "y": 2370,
   "w": 222,
   "h": 125,
   "children": [
    {
     "id": "tt024a",
     "type": "text",
     "x": 0,
     "y": 0,
     "w": 222,
     "h": 19.3,
     "text": "02 / Verb",
     "size": "s",
     "color": "mute"
    },
    {
     "id": "tt024b",
     "type": "text",
     "x": 0,
     "y": 20,
     "w": 222,
     "h": 22,
     "text": "EXTEND",
     "weight": 700
    },
    {
     "id": "tt024c",
     "type": "text",
     "x": 0,
     "y": 46,
     "w": 222,
     "h": 68,
     "text": "Stretch, add, reach beyond. Adding a perceptual channel to sense time passing.",
     "size": "s"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "tt025g",
   "type": "group",
   "x": 746,
   "y": 2370,
   "w": 222,
   "h": 125,
   "children": [
    {
     "id": "tt025a",
     "type": "text",
     "x": 0,
     "y": 0,
     "w": 222,
     "h": 19.3,
     "text": "03 / Adjective",
     "size": "s",
     "color": "mute"
    },
    {
     "id": "tt025b",
     "type": "text",
     "x": 0,
     "y": 20,
     "w": 222,
     "h": 22,
     "text": "PANORAMIC",
     "weight": 700
    },
    {
     "id": "tt025c",
     "type": "text",
     "x": 0,
     "y": 46,
     "w": 222,
     "h": 68,
     "text": "Whole, wide, all at once. Perceiving elapsed time and remaining time in the periphery.",
     "size": "s"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "tt026b",
   "type": "box",
   "fill": "faint",
   "round": 8,
   "x": 270,
   "y": 2530,
   "w": 698,
   "h": 50,
   "text": "Making the passage and structure of time more perceptible."
  },
  {
   "id": "tt030t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 32,
   "y": 2680,
   "w": 222,
   "h": 25.2,
   "text": "problem",
   "color": "mute",
   "nav": "problem"
  },
  {
   "id": "tt031t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 270,
   "y": 2680,
   "w": 460,
   "h": 25.2,
   "text": "Losing hours while absorbed",
   "weight": 700
  },
  {
   "id": "tt032t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 270,
   "y": 2730,
   "w": 698,
   "h": 85,
   "text": "“I sit down to work for twenty minutes. I look up and it's been three hours.”",
   "size": "l",
   "bg": "accent"
  },
  {
   "id": "tt033t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 270,
   "y": 2860,
   "w": 460,
   "h": 80,
   "text": "Nothing interrupts you, you just never felt the time go. People with ADHD call this time blindness, and most students know a milder version of it. A friend of mine lives with the full version, and watching it up close was frustrating for both of us.",
   "size": "s"
  },
  {
   "id": "tt034t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 270,
   "y": 2965,
   "w": 460,
   "h": 60,
   "text": "Clocks, timers, and calendars all work. But each requires remembering to look. And looking is least likely exactly when you are most absorbed.",
   "size": "s"
  },
  {
   "id": "tt035b",
   "type": "box",
   "fill": "line",
   "round": 8,
   "x": 270,
   "y": 3060,
   "w": 698,
   "h": 115,
   "text": "<span class=\"c-mute sz-s\">Problem statement</span><br><br><span class=\"w-700\">How might we help students become more aware of time passing while they're absorbed in their work, so they notice drift before it costs them?</span>"
  },
  {
   "id": "tt040t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 32,
   "y": 3300,
   "w": 222,
   "h": 25.2,
   "text": "secondary research",
   "color": "mute",
   "nav": "secondary research"
  },
  {
   "id": "tt041t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 270,
   "y": 3300,
   "w": 460,
   "h": 25.2,
   "text": "Time perception and music as an interface",
   "weight": 700
  },
  {
   "id": "tt042g",
   "type": "group",
   "x": 270,
   "y": 3360,
   "w": 341,
   "h": 140,
   "children": [
    {
     "id": "tt042a",
     "type": "text",
     "x": 0,
     "y": 0,
     "w": 341,
     "h": 45,
     "text": "Pleasant music shortens perceived time",
     "weight": 700
    },
    {
     "id": "tt042b",
     "type": "text",
     "x": 0,
     "y": 50,
     "w": 341,
     "h": 58,
     "text": "Tempo and pleasantness distort time judgment. Pleasant music makes durations feel shorter—which is why waiting rooms play it.",
     "size": "s"
    },
    {
     "id": "tt042c",
     "type": "text",
     "x": 0,
     "y": 115,
     "w": 341,
     "h": 20,
     "text": "Droit-Volet et al. (2013), Frontiers in Psychology",
     "size": "s",
     "color": "mute"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "tt043g",
   "type": "group",
   "x": 627,
   "y": 3360,
   "w": 341,
   "h": 140,
   "children": [
    {
     "id": "tt043a",
     "type": "text",
     "x": 0,
     "y": 0,
     "w": 341,
     "h": 45,
     "text": "Consistent timing deficits in ADHD",
     "weight": 700
    },
    {
     "id": "tt043b",
     "type": "text",
     "x": 0,
     "y": 50,
     "w": 341,
     "h": 58,
     "text": "A meta-analysis of 55 studies confirms significant timing deficits across duration discrimination and reproduction tasks.",
     "size": "s"
    },
    {
     "id": "tt043c",
     "type": "text",
     "x": 0,
     "y": 115,
     "w": 341,
     "h": 20,
     "text": "Marx et al. (2021), JAACAP",
     "size": "s",
     "color": "mute"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "tt044g",
   "type": "group",
   "x": 270,
   "y": 3520,
   "w": 341,
   "h": 140,
   "children": [
    {
     "id": "tt044a",
     "type": "text",
     "x": 0,
     "y": 0,
     "w": 341,
     "h": 45,
     "text": "Background music as an ADHD study habit",
     "weight": 700
    },
    {
     "id": "tt044b",
     "type": "text",
     "x": 0,
     "y": 50,
     "w": 341,
     "h": 58,
     "text": "Young adults with ADHD report listening to background music while studying significantly more than neurotypical peers, preferring stimulating tracks.",
     "size": "s"
    },
    {
     "id": "tt044c",
     "type": "text",
     "x": 0,
     "y": 115,
     "w": 341,
     "h": 20,
     "text": "Lachance, Pelland-Goulet & Gosselin (2024)",
     "size": "s",
     "color": "mute"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "tt045g",
   "type": "group",
   "x": 627,
   "y": 3520,
   "w": 341,
   "h": 140,
   "children": [
    {
     "id": "tt045a",
     "type": "text",
     "x": 0,
     "y": 0,
     "w": 341,
     "h": 45,
     "text": "Tempo communicates urgency without volume",
     "weight": 700
    },
    {
     "id": "tt045b",
     "type": "text",
     "x": 0,
     "y": 50,
     "w": 341,
     "h": 58,
     "text": "Acoustic rate is the most efficient parameter communicating urgency. Speeding up makes time feel heavier, while volume only adds annoyance.",
     "size": "s"
    },
    {
     "id": "tt045c",
     "type": "text",
     "x": 0,
     "y": 115,
     "w": 341,
     "h": 20,
     "text": "Hellier, Edworthy & Dennis (1993), Ergonomics",
     "size": "s",
     "color": "mute"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "tt046t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 270,
   "y": 3700,
   "w": 698,
   "h": 75,
   "text": "The music they study to is the very thing making their time disappear.",
   "size": "l",
   "bg": "accent"
  },
  {
   "id": "tt050t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 32,
   "y": 3920,
   "w": 222,
   "h": 25.2,
   "text": "precedents",
   "color": "mute",
   "nav": "precedents"
  },
  {
   "id": "tt051t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 270,
   "y": 3920,
   "w": 460,
   "h": 25.2,
   "text": "What already exists",
   "weight": 700
  },
  {
   "id": "tt052g",
   "type": "group",
   "x": 270,
   "y": 3975,
   "w": 222,
   "h": 135,
   "children": [
    {
     "id": "tt052a",
     "type": "text",
     "x": 0,
     "y": 0,
     "w": 222,
     "h": 19.3,
     "text": "01 / Takt (CHI 2016)",
     "size": "s",
     "color": "mute"
    },
    {
     "id": "tt052b",
     "type": "text",
     "x": 0,
     "y": 20,
     "w": 222,
     "h": 22,
     "text": "Wearable haptic pulse",
     "weight": 700
    },
    {
     "id": "tt052c",
     "type": "text",
     "x": 0,
     "y": 46,
     "w": 222,
     "h": 77.9,
     "text": "Taught: sensing time through the body. Shortfall: a steady pulse fades into the background through sensory habituation.",
     "size": "s"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "tt053g",
   "type": "group",
   "x": 508,
   "y": 3975,
   "w": 222,
   "h": 135,
   "children": [
    {
     "id": "tt053a",
     "type": "text",
     "x": 0,
     "y": 0,
     "w": 222,
     "h": 19.3,
     "text": "02 / Endel & Brain.fm",
     "size": "s",
     "color": "mute"
    },
    {
     "id": "tt053b",
     "type": "text",
     "x": 0,
     "y": 20,
     "w": 222,
     "h": 22,
     "text": "Generative focus audio",
     "weight": 700
    },
    {
     "id": "tt053c",
     "type": "text",
     "x": 0,
     "y": 46,
     "w": 222,
     "h": 77.9,
     "text": "Taught: soundscapes anchor deep work. Shortfall: Pomodoro timer sits beside music; sound itself doesn't carry time.",
     "size": "s"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "tt054g",
   "type": "group",
   "x": 746,
   "y": 3975,
   "w": 222,
   "h": 135,
   "children": [
    {
     "id": "tt054a",
     "type": "text",
     "x": 0,
     "y": 0,
     "w": 222,
     "h": 19.3,
     "text": "03 / Time Timer",
     "size": "s",
     "color": "mute"
    },
    {
     "id": "tt054b",
     "type": "text",
     "x": 0,
     "y": 20,
     "w": 222,
     "h": 22,
     "text": "Physical shrinking disk",
     "weight": 700
    },
    {
     "id": "tt054c",
     "type": "text",
     "x": 0,
     "y": 46,
     "w": 222,
     "h": 77.9,
     "text": "Taught: glanceable remaining time. Shortfall: requires direct line-of-sight; fails when absorbed in work on screen.",
     "size": "s"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "tt055b",
   "type": "box",
   "fill": "line",
   "round": 8,
   "x": 270,
   "y": 4140,
   "w": 698,
   "h": 60,
   "text": "The open space: an object that doesn't just tell you, but lets you feel how far through a session you are, using sound."
  },
  {
   "id": "tt060t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 32,
   "y": 4340,
   "w": 222,
   "h": 25.2,
   "text": "principles",
   "color": "mute",
   "nav": "principles"
  },
  {
   "id": "tt061t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 270,
   "y": 4340,
   "w": 460,
   "h": 25.2,
   "text": "From research to design",
   "weight": 700
  },
  {
   "id": "tt062g",
   "type": "group",
   "x": 270,
   "y": 4395,
   "w": 222,
   "h": 125,
   "children": [
    {
     "id": "tt062a",
     "type": "text",
     "x": 0,
     "y": 0,
     "w": 222,
     "h": 19.3,
     "text": "01",
